<v Matt Gentry>[MUSIC - "DON'T DO IT" BY RUSTY YORK AND WILLARD HALE]
<v Matt Gentry>（音乐 - 鲁斯蒂·约克和威拉德·黑尔演唱的《别做那件事》）

00:47:00.030 --> 00:47:15.760
<v Ira Glass>Act Three, Out of the Woods. OK, this last story is about a moose-- that's right, a moose-- who does not just do the one thing that you probably shouldn't do as a moose, he does, like, a series of them. This story comes from Ben Loory.
<v Ira Glass>第三幕，走出森林。好的，这最后一个故事是关于一只麋鹿——没错，一只麋鹿——它不仅做了一件你可能作为麋鹿不该做的事，它做了，比如，一系列这样的事。这个故事来自本·卢里（Ben Loory）。

00:47:15.760 --> 00:47:30.960
<v Ben Loory>A moose is standing in the forest when he suddenly hears a noise. He looks up and sees a plane flying overhead. As he watches, a man jumps out. A parachute bursts open, and the man floats safely down.
<v Ben Loory>一只麋鹿站在森林里，突然听到一阵噪音。它抬头看到一架飞机在头顶飞过。当它看着时，一个男人跳了出来。降落伞爆开，男人安全地飘落下来。

00:47:30.960 --> 00:47:48.300
<v Ben Loory>The moose goes over and looks at him. "Hello," says the man, gathering in his parachute. "Hello," says the moose. "What are you doing?" "Oh, nothing," says the man, "nothing much. I just jump out of planes every now and then."
<v Ben Loory>麋鹿走过去看着他。“你好，”男人一边收降落伞一边说。“你好，”麋鹿说。“你在做什么？”“噢，没什么，”男人说，“没什么大不了的。我只是偶尔从飞机上跳下来。”

00:47:48.300 --> 00:48:09.510
<v Ben Loory>The moose looks up at the sky. "Is it fun?" he says. "Oh, yes," says the man. "Have you never done it?" "Me?" says the moose. "Oh, no." "Well, come along with me," says the man. "We'll go back to town and get you all suited up, and then off we'll go. What do you say?"
<v Ben Loory>麋鹿抬头看向天空。“很有趣吗？”它说。“噢，是的，”男人说。“你从来没做过吗？”“我？”麋鹿说。“噢，不。”“好吧，跟我一起来，”男人说。“我们回镇上把你打扮好，然后我们就走。你觉得怎么样？”

00:48:09.510 --> 00:48:26.730
<v Ben Loory>"I don't know," says the moose. "Isn't it dangerous?" "Dangerous?" says the man. "No, not at all. Well, a little, but hey, isn't everything?" "I guess," says the moose, "when you put it that way."
<v Ben Loory>“我不知道，”麋鹿说。“这危险吗？”“危险？”男人说。“不，一点也不。嗯，有一点，但嘿，什么事不是呢？”“我想是吧，”麋鹿说，“当你这么说的时候。”

00:48:26.730 --> 00:48:44.940
<v Ben Loory>And after a while, he starts to nod. "All right," he says, "OK." "Great," says the man. "You're going to love it." And he claps the moose on the back, and the two of them start off.
<v Ben Loory>过了一会儿，它开始点头。“好吧，”它说，“好的。”“太棒了，”男人说。“你会喜欢它的。”他拍了拍麋鹿的后背，两人开始了出发。

00:48:44.940 --> 00:49:06.110
<v Ben Loory>When they get to the edge of the city, the moose suddenly stops. "What about the people?" he says. "What about them?" says the man. "Well," says the moose, "I'm not saying that I'm afraid of them, understand. But they're always out in the woods looking at me. It makes me nervous. I don't know what they want."
<v Ben Loory>当他们到达城市边缘时，麋鹿突然停了下来。“那人们呢？”它说。“他们怎么了？”男人说。“嗯，”麋鹿说，“我不是说我怕他们，你要明白。但他们总是在树林里盯着我看。这让我很紧张。我不知道他们想要什么。”

00:49:06.110 --> 00:49:26.700
<v Ben Loory>"Hm," says the man. "I doubt they want anything. But OK, here's what we'll do." He takes an extra t-shirt and hat out of his bag. "Put these on. Nobody will recognize you," he says. The moose looks at the offered disguise for a moment. "All right," he says, and puts it on.
<v Ben Loory>“嗯，”男人说。“我怀疑他们想要什么。但好吧，我们这样做。”他从包里拿出一件额外的T恤和帽子。“把这些穿上。没人会认出你，”他说。麋鹿看着提供的伪装片刻。“好吧，”它说，穿上了它们。

00:49:26.700 --> 00:49:39.150
<v Ben Loory>The man and the moose wander into town. The moose is very, very nervous. "Hey, Tom," someone says, and a group of people come over. "How'd your jump go today, and who's that?"
<v Ben Loory>男人和麋鹿走进了镇上。麋鹿非常非常紧张。“嘿，汤姆，”有人说，一群人走了过来。“你今天的跳伞怎么样，那是谁？”

00:49:39.150 --> 00:49:54.040
<v Ben Loory>The man turns and looks at the moose. "This is my friend, Lawrence," he says. "He just came in from the coast." "Quite a grip you've got there, Lawrence," says one of the men. "Are you bringing Lawrence to the party?" says another.
<v Ben Loory>男人转过身看着麋鹿。“这是我的朋友，劳伦斯（Lawrence），”他说。“他刚从海岸过来。”“你真有劲，劳伦斯，”其中一个人说。“你要带劳伦斯去派对吗？”另一个人说。

00:49:54.040 --> 00:50:17.370
<v Ben Loory>"Shoot," says the man, looking at the moose. "I completely forgot about that. You mind coming along to this thing tonight? It's sort of a shindig for my most recent jump." "Sure," says the moose, feeling self-conscious, "Sure. That'll be fine."
<v Ben Loory>“该死，”男人看着麋鹿说。“我完全忘了那件事。你介意今晚参加这个吗？这算是为我最近一次跳伞举办的小型聚会。”“当然，”麋鹿感到不自然地说，“当然。那没问题。”

00:50:17.370 --> 00:50:29.720
<v Ben Loory>That night the man and the moose go to the party. It is at the Explorers Club. There are a number of long tables arranged in a square. The man and the moose are in the place of honor.
<v Ben Loory>那天晚上男人和麋鹿去了派对。在探险家俱乐部。有几张长桌排成一个正方形。男人和麋鹿在荣誉席上。

00:50:29.720 --> 00:50:45.610
<v Ben Loory>The moose is having a wonderful time. The food is really very good. Different people make different speeches, and the moose finds the waitress quite fascinating.
<v Ben Loory>麋鹿玩得很开心。食物真的很好。不同的人发表了不同的演讲，麋鹿觉得女服务员很迷人。

00:50:45.610 --> 00:51:08.350
<v Ben Loory>But then, suddenly, something draws his attention-- heads, animal heads. They're lining the walls all around the top-- lion, zebra, deer, elk, and moose. Fear grips the moose's heart. "Killers," he thinks, looking around the room.
<v Ben Loory>但突然，有什么东西吸引了它的注意力——头，动物的头。它们沿着墙壁顶部排列——狮子、斑马、鹿、麋鹿和驯鹿。恐惧抓住了麋鹿的心。“杀手，”它心想，环顾房间。

00:51:08.350 --> 00:51:24.840
<v Ben Loory>"What is it?" says the man, sensing trouble. The moose turns and looks at him in horror. "You're trying to kill me," he says, his voice a whisper. "You brought me here to kill me." "What?" says the man. "Why would I do that? I don't understand."
<v Ben Loory>“怎么了？”男人说，感觉到麻烦。麋鹿转头看着他，满脸恐惧。“你想杀了我，”它说，声音轻得像耳语。“你带我到这里来杀我。”“什么？”男人说。“我为什么要那样做？我不明白。”

00:51:24.840 --> 00:51:34.250
<v Ben Loory>But the moose is too scared to explain. He stumbles backward to his feet. He points a hoof at the abomination on the wall.
<v Ben Loory>但麋鹿太害怕了，无法解释。它踉跄着后退站稳。它伸出蹄子指着墙上的那个可憎之物。

00:51:34.250 --> 00:51:51.340
<v Ben Loory>The man sees it, then his eyes go wide. "My god," he says, "I just didn't think." He reaches out to reassure the moose, but his hand grabs the t-shirt, and it rips and falls off. And then, to make matters worse, the moose's hat tumbles to the floor.
<v Ben Loory>男人看到了它，然后眼睛瞪大了。“天哪，”他说，“我就是没想到。”他伸出手安抚麋鹿，但他的手抓住了T恤，它撕破并掉了下来。然后，更糟糕的是，麋鹿的帽子掉到了地板上。

00:51:51.340 --> 00:52:19.840
<v Ben Loory>Everybody turns. "A moose," they cry. "Get him. Get him. Get the guns." The moose takes off. He galumphs out of the ballroom, knocking people over left and right. He barrels through the doors and off down the hall. The members of the Explorers Club are striking the glass on the gun cases. "Hurry," they are yelling, "It's a big one, the biggest."
<v Ben Loory>每个人都转过身。“一只麋鹿，”他们大喊。“抓住他。抓住他。去拿枪。”麋鹿跑开了。它笨拙地跳出宴会厅，左冲右撞地把人撞倒。它撞开门，冲进走廊。探险家俱乐部的成员正在敲碎枪柜上的玻璃。“快，”他们大喊，“这是一个大家伙，最大的。”

00:52:19.840 --> 00:52:29.590
<v Ben Loory>The moose careens out into the street. He's weaving in and out of cars. There's honking and screaming. The moose has never been so terrified.
<v Ben Loory>麋鹿狂奔到街上。它在汽车之间穿梭。到处是喇叭声和尖叫声。麋鹿从未如此害怕。

00:52:29.590 --> 00:52:43.490
<v Ben Loory>"Wait, wait," cries a voice. The moose looks back. It's the man running after him. "I'm sorry," yells the man. "I didn't think. I'm so stupid. I'll make it up to you. I'll get you out of this, I swear."
<v Ben Loory>“等等，等等，”一个声音叫道。麋鹿回头看。那是男人在后面追。“我很抱歉，”男人大喊。“我没想到。我太蠢了。我会补偿你的。我会带你走出这个境地，我发誓。”

00:52:43.490 --> 00:53:01.700
<v Ben Loory>"Are you kidding?" yells the moose. "Why should I trust you?" Just then, gunfire erupts. It's the Explorers Club hot on their trail. Bullets whiz past, close, closer. "I can take you to the plane," says the man. "It's your only chance."
<v Ben Loory>“你在开玩笑吗？”麋鹿大喊。“我为什么要信任你？”就在这时，枪声爆发了。那是探险家俱乐部在紧追不舍。子弹呼啸而过，很近，更近了。“我可以带你去飞机，”男人说。“这是你唯一的机会。”

00:53:01.700 --> 00:53:23.710
<v Ben Loory>The moose thinks. Another bullet whizzes by. "All right," the moose yells. "Climb on." The man jumps on, and the two of them charge through the streets. "Turn left," yells the man, and the moose turns. Up ahead is the airfield, behind, the men with guns, getting closer with every passing second.
<v Ben Loory>麋鹿思考着。另一颗子弹呼啸而过。“好吧，”麋鹿大喊。“爬上来。”男人跳上去，两人穿过街道。“向左转，”男人大喊，麋鹿转弯了。前方就是机场，身后，拿枪的人，每一秒钟都在接近。

00:53:23.710 --> 00:53:39.600
<v Ben Loory>"There's the plane," the man hollers, and the two dive on board. The man guns it, and the plane taxis toward the runway. Behind them, the Explorers Club lines up in a row. "Fire," says the leader. "Fire more."
<v Ben Loory>“那是飞机，”男人大叫，两人跳了上去。男人踩油门，飞机向跑道滑行。在他们身后，探险家俱乐部排成一行。“开火，”领导者说。“继续开火。”

00:53:39.600 --> 00:54:02.360
<v Ben Loory>The plane is hit in 10,000 places, but still, it manages to lift off. Behind it trails a cloud of smoke and fire that is terrifying to behold. "We're not going to make it!" the man yells to the moose. "We're going to have to jump." He turns and looks for the parachutes, but there is only one.
<v Ben Loory>飞机在10000个地方被击中，但它仍然设法起飞。身后拖着一团烟火，看起来非常恐怖。“我们要撑不住了！”男人对麋鹿大喊。“我们必须跳机。”他转身寻找降落伞，但只有一个。

00:54:02.360 --> 00:54:18.900
<v Ben Loory>"You take it," says the man, pushing it to the moose. But the moose just stares at it in silence. "No, you," says the moose. "I don't even know how to use it. Besides, I wouldn't have gotten this far without you."
<v Ben Loory>“你拿去吧，”男人说，把它塞给麋鹿。但麋鹿只是沉默地盯着它。“不，你拿，”麋鹿说。“我甚至不知道怎么用它。再说，没有你我走不到这一步。”

00:54:18.900 --> 00:54:27.440
<v Ben Loory>The man thinks for a moment. "We go together," he finally says. "It might work. It might not. Who knows?"
<v Ben Loory>男人思考片刻。“我们一起，”他最终说。“可能会成功。可能不会。谁知道呢？”

00:54:27.440 --> 00:54:44.310
<v Ben Loory>He straps the parachute around them both and edges the moose toward the door. "On the count of three," the man says. And the moose jumps.
<v Ben Loory>他把降落伞绑在两人身上，把麋鹿挪向舱门。“数到三，”男人说。然后麋鹿跳了下去。

00:54:44.310 --> 00:55:00.670
<v Ben Loory>The man and the moose plummet through the air. "Is that the forest," the moose calls, "down there?" "Yes," says the man. "Isn't it pretty?" "It is," says the moose. "I can see why you like doing this."
<v Ben Loory>男人和麋鹿在空中坠落。“那是森林吗，”麋鹿问道，“在下面？”“是的，”男人说。“不漂亮吗？”“是啊，”麋鹿说。“我明白你为什么喜欢这么做了。”

00:55:00.670 --> 00:55:23.230
<v Ben Loory>At this point, the ground is coming up pretty fast. "All right," says the man, "moment of truth." The two grip the pull cord tightly together. "I hope we can be friends," says the moose.
<v Ben Loory>此时，地面正迅速接近。“好吧，”男人说，“关键时刻到了。”两人紧紧握住拉绳。“希望我们能成为朋友，”麋鹿说。

00:55:23.230 --> 00:55:31.890
<v Ira Glass>Ben Loory-- so good, right-- reading a story from his collection of short fiction. It's called Stories for Nighttime and Some for the Day.
<v Ira Glass>本·卢里——太棒了，对吧——读着他短篇小说集中的一个故事。它叫《夜间故事与一些白日故事》（Stories for Nighttime and Some for the Day）。

